oxed (0.2.0~dev1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Establish the OxCaml terminal editor foundation.
    - Implement asynchronous application lifecycle and cleanup.
    - Integrate Lambda-term for keyboard input and rendering.
    - Integrate Zed for Unicode text buffers and editing.
    - Support opening existing files and unnamed buffers.

  * Introduce the oxed command interface.
    - Use λ as the Unicode command prompt.
    - Support keyboard-driven command entry and submission.
    - Implement p for printing and n for numbered output.
    - Parse absolute line addresses and compound ranges.
    - Represent dot as a half-open Unicode selection range.
    - Support beginning-of-buffer and end-of-file addressing.

  * Implement foundational editing operations.
    - Insert Unicode characters.
    - Move the editing cursor.
    - Delete characters forward and backward.
    - Preserve UTF-8 text during file loading.

  * Improve terminal behavior.
    - Position the physical cursor at the command prompt.
    - Restore terminal state after normal and exceptional exits.
    - Support Ctrl-Q for application termination.

  * Adopt Sam-style structural editing as the design direction.
    - Retain Ed as the command interpreter.
    - Prefer composable regular expressions over mandatory
      language-specific syntax parsers.
    - Reserve mouse interaction for an optional setting.
    - Defer Tree-sitter and LSP integration.

  * Add native build and regression tests.
    - Verify terminal lifecycle and cleanup.
    - Verify Unicode buffer initialization and editing.
    - Verify command parsing, numbered output, and dot semantics.

 -- EAX <info@dst9.org>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500

